{
 "voice": "am_puck",
 "duration": 65.38,
 "lines": [
  {
   "line": 0,
   "text": "What if every person on Earth jumped at exactly the same time? Could we shove the planet off course?",
   "start": 0.25,
   "end": 6.07
  },
  {
   "line": 1,
   "text": "There are eight point two billion of us, weighing about four hundred million tonnes all together.",
   "start": 6.51,
   "end": 11.645
  },
  {
   "line": 2,
   "text": "So we all squeeze into one place. Packed shoulder to shoulder, everybody fits in a space not much bigger than London.",
   "start": 11.965,
   "end": 18.8
  },
  {
   "line": 3,
   "text": "Three.",
   "start": 19.16,
   "end": 19.865
  },
  {
   "line": 4,
   "text": "Two.",
   "start": 20.085,
   "end": 20.69
  },
  {
   "line": 5,
   "text": "One.",
   "start": 20.91,
   "end": 21.54
  },
  {
   "line": 6,
   "text": "Jump!",
   "start": 21.8,
   "end": 22.455
  },
  {
   "line": 7,
   "text": "Eight billion people leave the ground, and the whole Earth moves...",
   "start": 22.795,
   "end": 26.19
  },
  {
   "line": 8,
   "text": "by less than a thousandth of the width of an atom.",
   "start": 26.43,
   "end": 28.96
  },
  {
   "line": 9,
   "text": "Because the planet is fifteen trillion times heavier than all of us put together.",
   "start": 29.32,
   "end": 33.625
  },
  {
   "line": 10,
   "text": "It's like a flea jumping off a cruise ship. The ship doesn't even notice.",
   "start": 33.925,
   "end": 38.02
  },
  {
   "line": 11,
   "text": "Luckily, when we land, the Earth moves right back.",
   "start": 38.42,
   "end": 40.975
  },
  {
   "line": 12,
   "text": "Unluckily, the landing is loud. In twenty eleven, Seattle football fans celebrated a touchdown so hard, a seismometer recorded it as a small earthquake.",
   "start": 41.255,
   "end": 51.205
  },
  {
   "line": 13,
   "text": "Now picture a hundred and twenty thousand of those crowds landing at once.",
   "start": 51.525,
   "end": 55.58
  },
  {
   "line": 14,
   "text": "But the real disaster comes afterwards.",
   "start": 56.02,
   "end": 58.175
  },
  {
   "line": 15,
   "text": "Eight billion people, in one place, all trying to get home at the same time.",
   "start": 58.455,
   "end": 62.74
  },
  {
   "line": 16,
   "text": "And we already know how that ends.",
   "start": 63.1,
   "end": 64.78
  }
 ],
